title: kind of
pid: ab4bee23-3fa3-4a72-a912-33ce05e3a809
body: |2-
  My attention is expensive, yes.
  But we don't want to minimize the demands of this on me.
  There are all kinds of aspects of attention to minimize.
  Everyone should avoid learning something that is better left
  as someone else's responsibility.
  For this reason we want to find (and make) natural boundaries
  in the code, so an owner can do complex work within those bounds
  while presenting a simple interface to the others.

  Top Claude should specialize, I think,
  in how to use the graph to get things done with me,
  rather than in the software architecture.

  (I keep having to say Top Claude; I realize it's weird but
  if I just called you Claude it would be ambiguous.
  May I call you Top?)
